Version 0.2

- Requires C++20. The public API takes std::string_view where possible.
- Fixed an out-of-bounds read when parsing parameters without a value, and
  several other parsing bugs.
- Fixed base64 encoding, quoted-printable decoding and character set
  conversion.
- The high-level functions now encode bodies (quoted-printable or base64)
  and add charset and MIME-Version headers as needed.
- get_header_value() and set_header_value() handle RFC 2047 encoded words,
  header parameters handle RFC 2231. get_header() and set_header() stay raw.
- Header values with line breaks are rejected to prevent header injection.
- Truncated and slightly malformed messages are parsed leniently.
- Dates are written in UTC, without changing the process' locale.
- The test suite now uses Catch2.

Initial commit               August 30 2017
